## Overview
What {{name}} is for, its entities and their ids, and anything important that is not in state.

## Context model
What one context represents and which service it runs; this scaffold is one context running one service.

## Getting started
The first calls in order: create a context for this app, then call `set` to store the first value.

## Procedures
### Store and read a value
Call `set` with a key and a value, then `get` with the key. Example: {"key":"hello","value":"world"}

## Rules and limits
Bounds, roles, rate limits and pitfalls, one per line; `get` on an unknown key fails with `NotFound`.
